      span: 65
      span: 4
      span: 20
      leading_comments: " TYPE_DEVSHM is not an OCI namespace: it is a per-group tmpfs,\n mounted once and reused, that sharing containers bind-mount their\n /dev/shm onto so writes through it are real shared memory (guest\n RAM), not just a shared IPC namespace identifier. It reuses this\n same create-once/reuse/path-return mechanism because the shape of\n the problem — and the \"only pay for it if actually requested\"\n requirement — is identical to the namespace types.\n"
    }
